    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class and it passes, along with the full build.\n\nDone. The change rejects creating an owner whose lower-cased email is already used by another owner, responding 409.\n\n**What I added:**\n- `RequireUniqueEmail` (function) \u2014 after email normalization, scans existing owners and throws `DuplicateEmailException` when the request's lower-cased email matches any existing owner's (normalized) email. An absent/blank email passes through, since email is optional.\n- `DuplicateEmailException` (checked exception) + `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing duplicate-telephone handling.\n- Escalation YAML mapping the exception to its handler.\n- Wired `requireUniqueEmail` into `owners.POST.yml` right after `normalizeEmail` (so the comparison uses the canonical lower-cased value) and before `requireUniqueTelephone`, under the same transaction governance.\n\nThis reuses the existing `OwnerEmails.normalize(...)` helper for canonicalization and follows the same single-responsibility, one-step-per-class pattern as the sibling `RequireUniqueTelephone`/`RequireUniqueHousehold` functions rather than adding logic to an existing class. Full test suite is green.",
